The test builds four `InlineQueryResultArticle` objects in `results` and passes them to `bot._effective_inline_results(...)`. In `ExtBot._effective_inline_results`, after calling `super()._effective_inline_results(...)`, the method loops over `effective_results`; since each article has `reply_markup` and the bot has callback-data caching enabled, the `else` branch runs each time and assigns `new_result = copy(result)`. That assignment happens before `new_result.reply_markup` is replaced, so each captured `new_result` value is just the copied original article for each of the four inputs, in order.

